body:
### Tested versions

4.7-dev3

### System information

Fedora 42

### Issue description

Noticed that the buttons for the various log entry types in the `EditorLog` scale differently based on what plugins are enabled/installed and when they are not.

The issue stems from the code inside `editor_log.cpp`, specifically this:
```cpp
	Button *button = type_filter_map[MSG_TYPE_STD]->toggle_button;
	button->set_button_icon(get_editor_theme_icon(SNAME("Popup")));
	button->set_custom_minimum_size(button->get_minimum_size_for_text_and_icon(wide_text, button->get_button_icon()) * EDSCALE);
	button = type_filter_map[MSG_TYPE_ERROR]->toggle_button;
	button->set_button_icon(get_editor_theme_icon(SNAME("StatusError")));
	button->set_custom_minimum_size(button->get_minimum_size_for_text_and_icon(wide_text, button->get_button_icon()) * EDSCALE);
	button = type_filter_map[MSG_TYPE_WARNING]->toggle_button;
	button->set_button_icon(get_editor_theme_icon(SNAME("StatusWarning")));
	button->set_custom_minimum_size(button->get_minimum_size_for_text_and_icon(wide_text, button->get_button_icon()) * EDSCALE);
	button = type_filter_map[MSG_TYPE_EDITOR]->toggle_button;
	button->set_button_icon(get_editor_theme_icon(SNAME("Edit")));
	button->set_custom_minimum_size(button->get_minimum_size_for_text_and_icon(wide_text, button->get_button_icon()) * EDSCALE);
```
We can see that the buttons are scaled based on the text/icon size, which, on the surface, makes perfect sense. But if you then take a look more closely at the implementation inside `button.cpp`, we'll see this:

```cpp
return (theme_cache.align_to_largest_stylebox ? _get_largest_stylebox_size() : _get_current_stylebox()->get_minimum_size()) + minsize;
```

Because `align_to_largest_stylebox` is enabled by default, buttons scale differently.


### Steps to reproduce

1. Start with an empty project, set display scale to 200% for easier identification.
2. Make project window as small as it will go, and take a screen shot of the editor log buttons, and take note of their custom min size.
3. Install any plugin that creates its own StyleBoxes, particularly where its StyleBoxes are larger than the editor's defaults.
4. Take note again of the buttons in the editor log, their custom min sizes are much larger.

